WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.048 --> 00:00:11.928
Hi, welcome back to the
Wheel of Life at-home retreat,

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:18.768
where this horse race is almost finished.

00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:25.150
We've reached session 24 out of twenty-five sessions,

00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:33.408
and this session is called
"My Hair on Fire,"

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:42.375
and the picture you see here is of a guy
with his clothes and his hair both on fire.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:50.925
Let's go to the Tibetan
and we can follow why we use this image.

00:00:54.929 --> 00:01:02.812
de na she tring le (DES NA BSHES SPRING LAS).
she tring (BSHES SPRING) means a famous book by Arya Nagarjuna.

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:11.029
It's called the "Letter to the King."
Sorry, "Letter to a Friend."

00:01:11.946 --> 00:01:16.951
His friend was King Udayibhadra,

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:22.707
and he sent this letter to the king.

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:31.633
I think it's interesting that Pabongka Rinpoche
quotes it so frequently in his lam rim (LAM RIM),

00:01:35.303 --> 00:01:42.268
because I had the good fortune
to work on that text a lot when I was very young.

00:01:45.313 --> 00:01:54.239
My friend Art Engle--a fellow student, a dear fellow student--and my teacher translated that book.

00:01:58.827 --> 00:02:03.832
And what I realized by studying that book

00:02:05.166 --> 00:02:08.378
is that it's a lam rim.

00:02:08.878 --> 00:02:16.761
So we tend to think that the lam rim, the steps of the path teaching, started in Tibet--but it's not true.

00:02:22.183 --> 00:02:26.729
This book in Sanskrit is called Suhrlekha (Suhṛllekha).

00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:36.865
It's by Nagarjuna, almost two thousand years ago,
and it's kind of a really beautiful lam rim.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:48.418
And Pabongka Rinpoche quotes two famous verses here.

00:02:49.919 --> 00:02:53.047
go-am gu la lobur me shor na
(MGO'AM GOS LA GLO BUR ME SHOR NA)

00:02:53.047 --> 00:02:57.510
Suppose suddenly your clothes
or your hair caught on fire.

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:05.894
And by the way, this happened with somebody
during my three year retreat.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:12.901
Somebody got too close to the fire,

00:03:14.611 --> 00:03:20.241
and their clothes caught on fire,
and it's very, very dangerous.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:25.914
So you have to actually--they taught us in the Boy Scouts

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:30.376
that you have to knock them down immediately,

00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:34.005
push them down,

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:38.134
and then roll them.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:45.099
So I did it.
de dak chir dok gyiwa tang ne kyang
(DE DAG PHYIR BZLOG BGYI BA BTANG NAS KYANG)

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:52.273
If your clothes or your hair catch on fire,
you're not going to do some other things.

00:03:55.276 --> 00:03:59.948
You're going to immediately do
whatever you can to stop the fire.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:07.789
Like you're not going to say,
"My hair's on fire, but I think I'll finish my coffee first."

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:15.338
We have a job like that.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:23.513
yang si mepar gyi (YANG SRID MED PAR BGYI)--
we want to put out the fire of rebirth.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:30.937
We have a very short time in this life.

00:04:32.146 --> 00:04:40.405
While you're healthy,
while you can still meditate,
while your mind is still clear,

00:04:40.905 --> 00:04:44.993
while you still have food and a place to stay,

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:53.876
you don't have time to do a lot of other things.
This fire is burning you now.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:05:02.510
So you have to stop everything else
and try to put out this fire.

00:05:04.679 --> 00:05:11.060
di le che chok dupa shen ma chi
('DI LAS CHES MCHOG DGOS PA GZHAN MA MCHIS)--
There's nothing more important that you have to do in your life.

00:05:14.939 --> 00:05:20.695
Generally, I have followed this in my life. Generally.

00:05:22.363 --> 00:05:29.912
And the fact is that if you want to put out that fire,

00:05:32.206 --> 00:05:37.920
you will not have time to do many other things.

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:46.554
So you might have to give up
many of the things that other people do in their life.

00:05:49.098 --> 00:05:53.936
And I've been doing that for almost fifty years,

00:05:55.855 --> 00:06:05.907
and I can report, I can tell you,
I think I made the right decision.

00:06:07.116 --> 00:06:14.999
So for example, I'm very bad
at buying birthday presents for my family.

00:06:18.336 --> 00:06:22.548
And it's not that I don't love them,
we love each other very much.

00:06:24.342 --> 00:06:32.350
But if I spend the time to go to the store to pick a gift for every family member--we have a big family--

00:06:36.187 --> 00:06:40.274
then I won't have time to do those three things:

00:06:40.525 --> 00:06:47.907
vipashyana--try to understand dependence and emptiness,

00:06:49.951 --> 00:06:58.960
shamatha--do my meditation practice every day without breaking it to go to the store to buy birthday presents,

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:09.637
and then the daily study and practice of morality
which I need to support my meditation.

00:07:12.473 --> 00:07:17.311
So Nagarjuna says here...

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:25.069
Nagarjuna says here,
"It's just like your hair is on fire."

00:07:26.863 --> 00:07:33.119
There's nothing else more important right now.
Put out that fire, then do other things.

00:07:35.538 --> 00:07:38.833
Become a Buddha, and then buy birthday gifts.

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:43.796
tsultrim dak dang (TSUL KHRIMS DAG DANG)--
how are you going to put out this fire?

00:07:45.006 --> 00:07:47.717
tsultrim dak dang sherab samten gyi
(TSUL KHRIMS DAG DANG SHES RAB BSAM GTAN GYIS)

00:07:48.342 --> 00:07:56.350
You should use tsultrim (TSUL KHRIMS), which means treating other people sweetly, nicely, not hurting other people,

00:07:58.936 --> 00:08:03.733
sherab (SHES RAB)--
that wisdom which understands emptiness...

00:08:06.027 --> 00:08:08.029
vipashyana is the highest form.

00:08:11.032 --> 00:08:16.037
And then shamatha,
a good steady state of meditation.

00:08:18.873 --> 00:08:23.753
If you remember,
these are the three parts of the woodcutter:

00:08:25.963 --> 00:08:28.883
sharp axe, which is wisdom;

00:08:30.927 --> 00:08:37.767
good focus, like that unshaking flame
to hit in the right place;

00:08:40.728 --> 00:08:46.067
and then two strong arms of morality to swing the axe.

00:08:48.903 --> 00:08:57.954
If you use those three, you will reach nyengende (MYA NGAN 'DAS). The text says nyengende--"Nirvana."

00:09:00.039 --> 00:09:03.918
Also called shiwa (ZHI BA),
which means "peace."

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:10.383
Also called dulwa (DUL BA), which means
you have "controlled yourself completely."

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:20.768
Also called drimepay go pang (DRI MED PA'I GO 'PHANG)--
"the state beyond all impurities."

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:29.151
Also called mi ga (MI RGA)--
you "don't have to get old anymore."

00:09:31.362 --> 00:09:34.865
mi chi (MI 'CHI) means that you "don't have to die anymore."

00:09:35.992 --> 00:09:43.165
se mi tsel (ZAD MI 'TSAL) means "this life and this purity will never end."

00:09:47.003 --> 00:09:54.302
In "The Letter to the Friend," the last line is strange.

00:09:55.803 --> 00:10:04.937
sa chu me lung nyi da drel tob dzu
(SA CHU ME RLUNG NYI ZLA BRAL THOB MDZOD)--
you should try to reach that place

00:10:06.147 --> 00:10:11.986
where you don't have earth, water, fire, and wind.

00:10:14.822 --> 00:10:20.161
And by the way, also get rid of the sun and the moon.

00:10:21.162 --> 00:10:29.879
Now for that last line,
I thought we should go on a little side trip,
which I like to do.

00:10:34.967 --> 00:10:40.348
What's that last line mean?
The other words for Nirvana are easy.

00:10:43.768 --> 00:10:48.105
Peace means, of course,
I don't have negative emotions anymore;
it's peaceful.

00:10:51.525 --> 00:10:54.862
Dulwa means "I'm self controlled."
Of course.

00:10:56.489 --> 00:11:01.577
dri ma mepa (DRI MA MED PA)--
no more problems in my body,
no more problems in my mind.

00:11:02.578 --> 00:11:10.544
Don't have to get old, don't have to die,
my pure life goes on forever.

00:11:11.253 --> 00:11:13.255
That's easy.

00:11:13.506 --> 00:11:20.680
But what's it mean--sa chu me lung nyi da drel--what's it mean to overcome earth, water, fire, wind,

00:11:22.014 --> 00:11:24.016
sun, and moon?

00:11:26.769 --> 00:11:29.855
I went to get you some commentaries.

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:36.904
The one I enjoyed the most
was by a great Mongolian author.

00:11:38.906 --> 00:11:42.702
His name is Chuje Ngawang Pelden.

00:11:43.911 --> 00:11:46.872
chuje (CHOS RJE) means "Dharma Lord."

00:11:48.958 --> 00:11:51.877
He lived about... I think two hundred years ago.

00:11:55.715 --> 00:11:59.552
Here's his commentary to that last line.

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:08.519
So we're going deeper, and that's what we do, and that's why this lam rim (LAM RIM) teaching is so slow!

00:12:10.938 --> 00:12:17.862
sa chu me lung nyi da drel top dzu--he says, "Now what about this strange last line?"

00:12:21.073 --> 00:12:24.118
So there's a Mongolian master,

00:12:26.203 --> 00:12:30.750
he says, "What about this strange last line?"

00:12:32.126 --> 00:12:36.756
He says, well sa chu me lung [SA CHU MED RLUNGS],
these four elements,

00:12:37.673 --> 00:12:43.053
that's easy. di la che ('DI LA BYED) means
"they refer to" the four elements.

00:12:44.346 --> 00:12:48.851
And it means after you reach Nirvana
or become a Buddha,

00:12:50.478 --> 00:12:53.647
you don't have this normal body

00:12:54.982 --> 00:12:58.194
made of these four elements.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:02.823
You have what we call a "rainbow body."

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.369
Why is it called rainbow body?

00:13:08.078 --> 00:13:15.419
From a distance, a rainbow looks like it has a shape
and it looks like it has colors.

00:13:17.213 --> 00:13:20.466
But then when you come up close to the rainbow,

00:13:21.217 --> 00:13:23.844
you can put your hand through it,

00:13:24.762 --> 00:13:28.182
and a Buddha's physical body is similar.

00:13:29.892 --> 00:13:35.231
Now here's the part that I like about his commentary,
it's very sweet.

00:13:36.357 --> 00:13:41.153
He says nyi dz (NYI ZLA).
Now why do they mention sun and the moon?

00:13:42.947 --> 00:13:46.325
kyepar pak tu le (KHYAD PAR 'PHAGS BSTOD LAS)--

00:13:47.201 --> 00:13:56.043
This is a famous book called
"The Extraordinary Praises" or something.
"Praise of the One Who is Extraordinarily Superior."

00:13:56.293 --> 00:13:59.004
It's a poem.

00:13:59.213 --> 00:14:02.049
[Xiaoping question inaudible]
No, he's going to quote, he's going to quote a book.

00:14:02.299 --> 00:14:10.057
It's a famous eulogy.
Eulogy means "a poem of praise," found in the Tengyur.

00:14:13.185 --> 00:14:15.104
And it says,

00:14:15.104 --> 00:14:26.073
ne tsu nyima ngul ne no (NE TZOS NYI MA BRNGOL NAS NO),
which is probably mistake--everything is misspelled and mis-carved here. I had to replace a lot of words.

00:14:27.157 --> 00:14:33.080
But he says, tarpa chipar she che drak
(THAR PA MCHIS PAR BSHAD CES GRAGS)--

00:14:33.789 --> 00:14:37.751
The parrot, the green parrot--the bird who talks,

00:14:39.503 --> 00:14:42.715
he poked the sun

00:14:45.092 --> 00:14:47.094
with his beak,

00:14:49.096 --> 00:14:52.808
and then they say he got to Nirvana.

00:14:54.101 --> 00:15:03.986
What's that all about?
This is supposed to explain "the sun and the moon." There's "no more sun, there's no more moon."

00:15:03.986 --> 00:15:05.988
Forget the sun and the moon.

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:13.120
drang song (DRANG SRONG) means "a Hindu saint."

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:21.337
He's called Gyepaybu (RGYAS PA'I BU).

00:15:22.588 --> 00:15:30.137
With some miracle powers,
he took a parrot or he became a parrot.
It's not clear.

00:15:32.473 --> 00:15:39.063
He flew to the sun and he poked a hole in the sun,

00:15:42.524 --> 00:15:50.115
and then that saint got into the hole
and he reached Nirvana.

00:15:50.491 --> 00:15:56.497
So this Mongol master--who is a great, great master--

00:15:58.666 --> 00:16:04.171
he says Shantideva's...,
oh sorry, Nagarjuna's book,

00:16:05.047 --> 00:16:14.098
they are criticizing this idea that Nirvana is some place on the other side of the moon or something like that.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:26.151
So he criticizes--he says "sun and moon"--when the book says "you are free of the sun and moon,"

00:16:26.151 --> 00:16:31.699
it means you are free of this dumb idea about what is Nirvana.

00:16:37.162 --> 00:16:48.549
I found another interesting...
yeah, here is a commentary by Rendawa.

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:56.724
Rendawa was a Sakya master
who was the teacher of Tsongkapa.

00:16:59.643 --> 00:17:02.563
And when he explains the sun and moon

00:17:03.188 --> 00:17:05.399
chi rulpa kachik (PHYI ROL PA KHA CIG)--some non-buddhists say.
yang chi rulpa kachik (YANG PHYI ROL PA KHA CIG).

00:17:05.399 --> 00:17:08.068
It's at the end of his quotation.

00:17:08.068 --> 00:17:20.164
kawa dung gya pu ba showa mo muk tik dok
(KHA BA DUNG RGYA SPOS BA ZHO BA MO MU TIG MDOG)

00:17:20.164 --> 00:17:26.462
It says some people think
when you reach Nirvana you go into some white light.

00:17:29.089 --> 00:17:32.760
It's like the color of snow,

00:17:32.926 --> 00:17:36.138
or the color of a white shell,

00:17:37.139 --> 00:17:42.144
Or like the color of pearl, or the color of yoghurt.

00:17:45.105 --> 00:17:49.234
And it looks like an umbrella covers you.

00:17:51.361 --> 00:17:55.616
And these are all weird ideas about Nirvana.

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:02.790
He says when this book says
"you go beyond the sun and the moon,"

00:18:05.667 --> 00:18:08.962
it means you go beyond these dumb ideas about

00:18:09.296 --> 00:18:15.511
"Nirvana is like a big umbrella that's colored white and you stay under the umbrella like in a donut of the sun."

00:18:35.155 --> 00:18:41.495
And you can say those are just stupid old ideas from some weird groups in India.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:49.128
But you might examine what ideas you have
about what is Nirvana,

00:18:53.674 --> 00:18:58.971
and maybe it's not much different
from the white umbrella.

00:19:02.391 --> 00:19:09.106
Now just for fun, which I enjoy doing,
I thought you would like to go to a...

00:19:09.523 --> 00:19:14.695
this is a book by Pabongka Rinpoche himself.

00:19:16.697 --> 00:19:22.202
And this is a beautiful kind of genre of book,
it's a type of literature.

00:19:24.204 --> 00:19:28.000
And it's called dri len (DRIS LAN).
dri len means "question and answer."

00:19:29.042 --> 00:19:34.715
So even in this course,
we're going to be doing a special master class,

00:19:37.509 --> 00:19:42.890
and I'll be accepting questions from you,
and I'll be giving answers live.

00:19:45.726 --> 00:20:01.575
Also in the expanded course, you'll be able to ask questions directly online or in person, or by internet to senior ACI teachers.

00:20:05.913 --> 00:20:13.837
But in ancient times,
somebody would sit there carving the question.

00:20:16.131 --> 00:20:25.098
So here's a question that somebody actually asked Pabongka Rinpoche,
probably about a hundred years ago.

00:20:26.433 --> 00:20:30.062
she tring le sa chu me lung nyi da drel top dzu
(BSHES SPRING LAS, SA CHU ME RLUNG NYI ZLA BRAL THOB MDZOD)--

00:20:30.103 --> 00:20:39.821
So what about that last line of "The Letter to a Friend," which talks about you reached Nirvana where you don't have sun and moon anymore?

00:20:43.992 --> 00:20:53.835
Oh, and here's Pabongka's own answer because he didn't answer it...
he didn't ask the question in his lam rim, but somebody asked him later, "What was that line?"

00:20:58.215 --> 00:21:09.851
And by the way, this is the great benefit of having five million pages
of scriptures digitalized in the last thirty-three years.

00:21:15.816 --> 00:21:24.283
And I know many of you watching this lam rim are helping to organize fundraising for that digitalization.

00:21:29.288 --> 00:21:31.873
I wanted to thank you for that.

00:21:31.873 --> 00:21:39.798
And the reason I can go deeper with you
is because of your fundraising.

00:21:41.008 --> 00:21:47.180
And it definitely helps poor people
around the world who we train.

00:21:47.472 --> 00:21:49.224
For thirty-three years.

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:59.276
And it's beautiful now, as some of those ladies that I met in the first year of this project,

00:22:00.694 --> 00:22:07.576
they had children, and now those children
are working next to them on the computer.

00:22:12.205 --> 00:22:18.545
Ok, so here it says, chi rolpa ga shik gi jungwa shi dang nyi da sok la top ja tartuk tu dzinpa dang
(PHYI ROL PA 'GA' ZHIG GIS 'BYUNG BA BZHI DANG NYI ZLA SOGS LA THOB BYA MTHAR THUG TU 'DZIN PA DANG)--

00:22:18.545 --> 00:22:25.344
It says "some people"--ancient weird schools--

00:22:27.387 --> 00:22:32.142
Tthey think Nirvana is like a white light
where you go and you stay in this white light."

00:22:37.731 --> 00:22:45.072
tarpa suk chen du dupa (THAR PA GZUGS CAN DU 'DOD PA)--
These are strange ideas that Nirvana is a physical place.

00:22:48.241 --> 00:22:52.079
But if you really want to go to the real Nirvana,

00:22:52.996 --> 00:22:55.916
You need those three trainings:

00:22:56.875 --> 00:22:58.794
morality,

00:22:58.919 --> 00:23:00.921
concentration,

00:23:01.088 --> 00:23:03.298
and wisdom.

00:23:06.093 --> 00:23:10.764
Yeah, I have to say, a lot of people think

00:23:11.807 --> 00:23:16.770
that if you study this section
that we've covered with twenty-five classes,

00:23:19.606 --> 00:23:21.608
if you study it well,

00:23:22.484 --> 00:23:25.070
then you will reach Nirvana.

00:23:25.987 --> 00:23:31.952
People think it's like you got very drunk.

00:23:33.995 --> 00:23:35.956
You are like this...

00:23:36.748 --> 00:23:38.750
for the rest of time...

00:23:39.042 --> 00:23:42.754
and you are just like in another space.

00:23:44.089 --> 00:23:47.134
This is not Nirvana at all.

00:23:47.676 --> 00:23:49.845
Nirvana's definition:

00:23:50.554 --> 00:24:01.106
nyondrip ma lupar pangpay sosor tak gok
(NYON SGRIB MA LUS PAR SPANGS PA'I SO SOR BRTAG 'GOG)--
You basically get rid of your anger, and jealousy,
and other negative emotions, forever.

00:24:04.109 --> 00:24:11.366
That's Nirvana.
So Xiaoping, for example,
yesterday she was translating for me here,

00:24:13.660 --> 00:24:17.831
and today she's translating for me here--same place.

00:24:19.332 --> 00:24:24.379
Then it's possible that she reached Nirvana last night.

00:24:25.589 --> 00:24:29.176
And she won't look any different.

00:24:30.177 --> 00:24:33.180
Okay, so you have to understand that.

00:24:33.972 --> 00:24:36.683
The person sitting next to you,

00:24:37.267 --> 00:24:43.106
they could have reached Nirvana last night
because of these great classes.

00:24:45.108 --> 00:24:50.322
And they're not going to change--
their outer appearance is not going to change.

00:24:51.198 --> 00:24:57.579
They don't have any more negative emotions
and you cannot make them angry.

00:25:00.373 --> 00:25:03.543
Okay, let's go back to lam rim.

00:25:04.377 --> 00:25:12.469
But that kind of going deeper is only possible because we have a database that we built for thirty-three years.

00:25:17.724 --> 00:25:22.187
I estimate we have a hundred and seventeen years to go,

00:25:25.148 --> 00:25:30.779
so I hope you will continue to help,
and I thank you for your help so far.

00:25:33.532 --> 00:25:37.077
Especially Gold Club friends.

00:25:39.204 --> 00:25:43.750
che sungpa tar kyebu dring gi nyam su lang ja ni
(CES GSUNGS PA LTAR, SKYES BU 'BRING GI NYAMS SU BLANG BYA NI)

00:25:43.875 --> 00:25:52.759
Well, what is it that people in this medium motivation--what are they trying to reach?

00:25:53.260 --> 00:25:59.891
They just want to stop suffering forever for themselves.

00:26:00.475 --> 00:26:03.979
Well, what should they be focusing on?

00:26:04.229 --> 00:26:11.194
hlakpay lappa sum (LHAG PA'I BSLAB PA GSUM)--
those three extraordinary trainings.

00:26:12.487 --> 00:26:15.115
Always being nice to other people.

00:26:16.241 --> 00:26:19.703
Doing your meditation every morning.

00:26:20.287 --> 00:26:24.374
And study, study, study about emptiness.

00:26:25.125 --> 00:26:32.882
sum yinpe kyebu chenpoy chu kor mi tri na kamdir lappa sum ka che gu
(GSUM YIN PAS SKYES BU CHEN PO'I CHOS SKOR MI 'KHRID NA SKABS 'DIR BSLAB PA GSUM KA 'CHAD DGOS)--

00:26:33.133 --> 00:26:41.057
Now, if I wasn't going to teach you guys
the highest tract, @Mahayana tract,

00:26:44.144 --> 00:26:51.693
if this was just a series of lectures
about how to reach Nirvana not Buddhahood--

00:26:55.071 --> 00:27:07.334
of course Buddhahood means your whole body changes, your whole mind changes, you're able to help people on billions of planets at the same time.

00:27:15.842 --> 00:27:24.225
Nirvana just means me, one person here on this couch,
I don't have anger, I don't have jealousy.

00:27:27.520 --> 00:27:32.942
Which by the way,
that means you got out of the wheel of Life.

00:27:35.612 --> 00:27:39.699
But not everybody who
reached Nirvana reached Buddhahood.

00:27:42.118 --> 00:27:45.163
Buddhahood, your whole being changes.

00:27:48.375 --> 00:27:56.132
And you are able to help countless beings
on countless planets at the same time.

00:27:59.219 --> 00:28:01.721
Then Pabongka Rinpoche says,

00:28:03.098 --> 00:28:08.478
I'm not done with you after I finish this Nirvana thing.

00:28:09.688 --> 00:28:12.148
I have a big plan for you.

00:28:12.941 --> 00:28:17.404
We're going to go to the greater way teachings, @Mahayana teachings,

00:28:18.113 --> 00:28:21.491
where you learn to become a Buddha.

00:28:22.200 --> 00:28:29.082
To get to that Buddhahood you're also
going to need these same three trainings.

00:28:31.042 --> 00:28:36.589
So if I wasn't going to teach you this highest path,

00:28:37.924 --> 00:28:41.261
If I was just teaching you about Nirvana,

00:28:41.720 --> 00:28:48.184
well then, I would teach you the details
of those three trainings today.

00:28:50.353 --> 00:28:56.609
But, I am going to teach you those higher goals,

00:28:57.652 --> 00:29:03.450
so I think we'll save two of those trainings for later.

00:29:04.951 --> 00:29:09.456
shamatha training--
deep meditation.

00:29:09.956 --> 00:29:15.211
vipashyana training--
special view of emptiness.

00:29:16.755 --> 00:29:20.341
I'll teach those to you guys later.

00:29:20.800 --> 00:29:24.345
And by the way, that's my plan also.

00:29:25.221 --> 00:29:35.231
After we finish this book, because Pabongka Rinpoche doesn't spend much time on shamatha and vispashyana in this book...a little bit, but not much,

00:29:43.156 --> 00:29:50.371
at the end of this book we're going to go to
"The Great Book on the Steps of the Path,"

00:29:52.373 --> 00:30:01.007
Lam Rim Chenmo (LAM RIM CHEN MO).
That will take us thirteen more years to finish.

00:30:03.760 --> 00:30:10.225
We will just do the part on shamatha and vipashyana.

00:30:14.646 --> 00:30:24.155
Okay, so I'm telling you, and Pabongka's telling you, We'll get to there later, those two trainings we'll cover later.

00:30:27.367 --> 00:30:35.166
So I'm going to tsultrim kyi lappa tsel du tun (TSUL KHRIMS KYI BSLAB PA RTZAL DU BTON) means "let's focus on ethical way of life."

00:30:38.795 --> 00:30:45.885
That's the chak she (PHYAG BZHES) here. chak she means "that's the high lamas' tradition at this point."

00:30:46.052 --> 00:30:52.225
We just focus on morality because we're going to teach you shamatha and vipashyana later.

00:30:55.144 --> 00:31:01.818
Then he quotes again, Nagarjuna's "Letter to a Friend."

00:31:03.069 --> 00:31:08.783
trim ni gyu dang mi gyuy sa shin du yunten kun gyi shi ten lakpar sung
(KHRIMS NI RGYU DANG MI RGYU'I SA BZHIN DU YON TAN KUN GYI GZHI RTEN LAGS PAR GSUNGS)

00:31:08.867 --> 00:31:15.290
How can I describe the practice of living an ethical life?

00:31:20.920 --> 00:31:31.139
Think about this planet Earth. The big dirt, the huge, huge, huge--all the countries are resting on this planet.

00:31:32.891 --> 00:31:37.186
gyu dang mi gyuy sa (RGYU DANG MI RGYU'I SA) is an old, old joke.

00:31:39.147 --> 00:31:46.988
The dirt of this planet holds up
everything that is moving
and everything that is not moving.

00:31:50.116 --> 00:31:54.078
So right now, we're in Sedona, Arizona.

00:31:54.829 --> 00:32:03.546
I don't know if you can see, but these red mountains
in the background are very, very famous.
Six million people a year come here to visit.

00:32:06.591 --> 00:32:12.388
And the earth patiently, quietly, holds up those mountains all day and all night.

00:32:18.603 --> 00:32:24.233
And if you look out the window here,
you can see some cars moving.

00:32:25.735 --> 00:32:30.573
And the earth patiently holds them up
all the time also--day and night.

00:32:33.368 --> 00:32:43.628
So whether things are moving like the cars,
or whether things are not moving like the red mountains, the earth is very patient. He just holds them up.

00:32:50.093 --> 00:32:55.181
And Nagarjuna says, "Your morality is like that."

00:32:56.224 --> 00:32:59.060
Okay, you you want to meditate,

00:32:59.727 --> 00:33:02.855
you want to see emptiness directly?

00:33:03.856 --> 00:33:07.360
By the way, the meditation is like the mountains,

00:33:08.611 --> 00:33:11.906
and the seeing emptiness directly is like the cars.

00:33:12.782 --> 00:33:21.374
But somebody patient, quiet, always there--
has to be under. Foundation.

00:33:25.545 --> 00:33:27.672
And that's morality.

00:33:28.047 --> 00:33:35.096
shepa tar yunten tamche kyi shi yinpe
(ZHES PA LTAR YON TAN THAMS CAD KYI GZHI YIN PAS)--
being nice to other people is the foundation of every good quality.

00:33:40.143 --> 00:33:49.444
tsultrim nampar dakpa gel che
(TSUL KHRIMS RNAM PAR DAG PA GAL CHE)--
therefore, never hurting any other person is extremely important

00:33:51.738 --> 00:33:58.244
di ni sanggye kyi tenpay tsawa
('DI NI SANGS RGYAS KYI BSTAN PA'I RTZA BA)--
treating other people nicely is the root of all Buddhism.

00:34:01.581 --> 00:34:06.335
sung na pen yun che (BSRUNG NA PHAN YON CHE)--
if you keep an ethical way of life,

00:34:06.335 --> 00:34:11.424
if you are nice to other people, the benefits that come to you are unbelievable.

00:34:15.595 --> 00:34:18.806
ma sung na nye mik kyang shintu che te
(MA BSRUNGS NA NYES DMIGS KYANG SHIN TU CHE STE)

00:34:18.806 --> 00:34:30.234
and if you don't keep to an ethical way of life, and you do hurt other people, you cannot imagine the kind of trouble you are making for yourself.

00:34:33.112 --> 00:34:41.454
And I'll tell you another important thing that
Buddha said about being nice to other people.

00:34:48.252 --> 00:34:56.219
If people in any city or country are keeping their commitment to be nice to other people,

00:35:00.932 --> 00:35:05.645
then Buddha said "Then Buddhism is there."

00:35:06.771 --> 00:35:12.652
And if they're not keeping those kinds of commitments to be nice to other people,

00:35:14.695 --> 00:35:19.492
then you cannot say Buddhism has reached that place.

00:35:23.538 --> 00:35:25.832
Then he repeats:

00:35:26.666 --> 00:35:29.752
gelong dulwa dzinpa tenpa yu la
(DGE SLONG 'DUL BA 'DZIN PA BSTAN PA YOD LA)

00:35:31.754 --> 00:35:35.967
If there's one person in a city

00:35:36.551 --> 00:35:45.059
keeping to a way of life where they never
hurt other people, then Buddhism exists in that city.

00:35:50.523 --> 00:35:58.281
Even if there's a @tantra--
high secret teaching,

00:35:58.322 --> 00:36:05.705
reach that city,
and everybody's ringing their bells...

00:36:07.957 --> 00:36:12.086
but if they're not being nice to other people,

00:36:13.087 --> 00:36:18.885
then we can say the Buddhist teachings
did not reach that place,

00:36:20.595 --> 00:36:26.559
even though people are practicing
the highest teaching there--but they are not moral.

00:36:32.940 --> 00:36:37.570
Therefore, the Buddha said himself,

00:36:38.196 --> 00:36:44.202
nga ni nyengende gyur na di ni kyu kyi tunpa she
(NGA NI MYA NGAN 'DAS GYUR NA,'DI NI KHYOD KYI STON PA ZHES)

00:36:45.620 --> 00:36:51.083
After I disappear from this world,
after I reach my final Nirvana,

00:36:54.253 --> 00:36:57.882
part of me will stay in this world.

00:36:58.507 --> 00:37:01.594
And that part of me will be your teacher forever.

00:37:03.554 --> 00:37:08.184
And that's keeping your vows
and not hurting other people.

00:37:08.559 --> 00:37:11.812
So if one person in this world

00:37:12.939 --> 00:37:17.818
is keeping their commitment never to hurt other people,

00:37:19.820 --> 00:37:25.785
then Buddha said, "You can say I'm still here."

00:37:27.453 --> 00:37:36.212
Final sentence of this series...

00:37:37.630 --> 00:37:42.343
and then the twenty-fifth session will be a review.

00:37:44.804 --> 00:37:51.811
So listen and let it be like a mantra for you.
Listen to the words.
It's a blessing

00:37:54.063 --> 00:37:56.691
rang gyu kyi tsultrim la tunpay ku tsab yin nyam du che tre che ne sun gu

00:37:56.691 --> 00:38:00.111
(RANG RGYUD KYI TSUL KHRIMS LA STON PA'I SKU TSAB YIN SNYAM DU GCES SPRAS BYAS NAS BSRUNG DGOS)

00:38:00.861 --> 00:38:08.869
So most of you listening,
you probably took some kind of Buddhist vows,

00:38:09.328 --> 00:38:12.873
at least the ten good deeds.

00:38:13.165 --> 00:38:15.084
No killing.

00:38:15.167 --> 00:38:16.836
No stealing.

00:38:17.128 --> 00:38:20.506
No hurting other people's relationships.

00:38:20.673 --> 00:38:21.841
Etcetera.

00:38:22.049 --> 00:38:26.262
We can say that in your mind stream,

00:38:27.847 --> 00:38:32.226
you are keeping this way of life

00:38:32.852 --> 00:38:35.646
where you are nice to other people.

00:38:37.356 --> 00:38:43.154
So then Pabongka says, so we can say,

00:38:44.363 --> 00:38:50.870
okay, you don't have to be perfect, but those of you who are trying to keep your six-times book,

00:38:52.246 --> 00:38:58.210
and since you heard about this teaching about seeds,

00:39:00.004 --> 00:39:04.008
you are trying to be nicer to other people,

00:39:05.384 --> 00:39:14.852
as long as you generally, imperfectly,
are trying to be nice to other people--
not perfectly,

00:39:16.354 --> 00:39:20.566
we can say the Buddha is alive inside of you.

00:39:22.735 --> 00:39:27.907
And che tre (GCES SPRAS) means "take good care" of that Buddha.

00:39:28.240 --> 00:39:31.786
It's most precious thing in your life.

00:39:32.495 --> 00:39:36.082
That's the end of session 24.

00:39:37.416 --> 00:39:44.715
In session 25, we're going to do a review
of the whole twenty-five sessions.

00:39:46.258 --> 00:39:47.927
We'll see you then.

00:39:48.094 --> 00:39:55.434
I know Xiaoping you're very tired, and you've been working very hard, and thank you for translating.

